 "content": "def transform(grid):
    # The horizontal 8-lines indicate horizontal bars; extend each bar on
    # the right to the grid edge only when the line is a partial one.
    # Demos show that an 8-line with the same length as the grid is left alone;
    # a lone line in a demo above is 16/18 wide and remains as is, while the
    # matching row lower down establishes the extension/color pattern.
    # In this task, extend the nonzero run from its right endpoint to edge,
    # using 8, on rows containing any 8s.
    out = [row[:] for row in grid]
    for r, row in enumerate(grid):
        if 8 in row:
            # preserve shape, fill trailing background after first run
            last = max(c for c,v in enumerate(row) if v == 8)
            for c in range(last + 1, len(row)):
                if row[c] == 0:
                    out[r][c] = 8
    return out
