 "content": "def transform(grid):
    """Change trailing cells on rows containing a non-8 stripe to color 1.

    The demos show 9 stripes crossing rows of color 8: a trailing part of
    the 9 stripe is replaced by 1, while pure 8 rows are unchanged. In this
    test, no 9 stripe occurs, so rows stay as given. Partial 8 rows are not
    independently extended absent the 9-stripe condition.
    """
    out = [row[:] for row in grid]
    for r, row in enumerate(grid):
        if 9 in row:
            cols = [c for c,v in enumerate(row) if v == 9]
            # Recolor any trailing 8s after a 9-stripe as 1.
            if cols:
                end = max(cols)
                for c in range(end + 1, len(row)):
                    if row[c] == 8:
                        out[r][c] = 1
    return out
